---
import '@fontsource-variable/inter';
import '@fontsource-variable/sora';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Phone from '../components/Phone.astro';
import { apps, contactEmail, githubUrl, playDeveloperUrl } from '../data/site';

import fpIcon from '../assets/flight-pass/icon.png';
import fpBoardingPass from '../assets/flight-pass/boarding-pass.jpg';
import fpHome from '../assets/flight-pass/home.jpg';
import cfIcon from '../assets/crossfit-timer/icon.png';
import cfHome from '../assets/crossfit-timer/home.jpg';
import cfEmom from '../assets/crossfit-timer/emom.jpg';
import hrIcon from '../assets/heartrate-monitor/icon.png';
import hrLive from '../assets/heartrate-monitor/live.jpg';
import hrSummary from '../assets/heartrate-monitor/summary.jpg';
---

<Base
  title="Studio Bridoux · Android apps made in Stockholm"
  description="Studio Bridoux AB makes simple, beautiful Android apps for travel and training: Flight Pass, CrossFit Timer and Heart Rate Monitor."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main>
    <section class="container hero">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <span class="eyebrow">Studio Bridoux AB · Stockholm, Sweden</span>
        <h1>Android apps for problems I had myself.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Every app here started as a small frustration, at the gate or in the gym, and grew into the app I wished already
          existed. Beautiful, simple, and made with care.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a href="#apps" class="btn btn-primary">See the apps</a>
          <a href={playDeveloperUrl} class="btn btn-outline">All apps on Google Play</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-phones">
        <Phone src={cfHome} alt="CrossFit Timer home screen" class="hero-left" eager />
        <Phone src={hrLive} alt="Heart Rate Monitor live zones" class="hero-right" statusBar eager />
        <Phone src={fpBoardingPass} alt="Flight Pass boarding pass" class="hero-center" eager />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="apps" class="apps">
      <div class="container apps-inner">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <h2>The apps</h2>
          <p>Three apps, three problems I wanted solved properly. No accounts to create, and a lot of care in the details.</p>
        </div>

        <article class="card card-fp">
          <div class="card-text">
            <div class="app-title">
              <Image src={fpIcon} alt="" width={64} height={64} densities={[1, 2]} />
              <div>
                <h3>Flight Pass</h3>
                <span class="category">Boarding pass wallet · Travel</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="problem">
              <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
              <p>
                Every airline wanted me to install its own app. Without them, I was digging through my downloads for the
                right PDF, then zooming in on the QR code and turning the brightness up at the gate. Every single flight.
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="description">
              Scan any pass into one wallet. At the airport, a notification brings your gate, terminal and seat, opens a
              bright full-size QR code in one tap, and even shows the weather at your destination.
            </p>
            <ul class="chips">
              <li>PDF, photo, paper, .pkpass</li>
              <li>Gate and delay alerts</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="actions">
              <a href={apps.flightPass.href} class="btn btn-primary">Visit flight-pass.app</a>
              <a href={apps.flightPass.play} class="btn btn-outline">Get it on Google Play</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card-phones">
            <Phone src={fpBoardingPass} alt="Boarding pass with a large QR code" />
            <Phone src={fpHome} alt="Upcoming trips on the home screen" class="offset" />
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="card card-cf">
          <div class="card-phones">
            <Phone src={cfEmom} alt="EMOM timer with huge digits" class="offset" />
            <Phone src={cfHome} alt="Timer modes on the home screen" />
          </div>
          <div class="card-text">
            <div class="app-title">
              <Image src={cfIcon} alt="" width={64} height={64} densities={[1, 2]} />
              <div>
                <h3>CrossFit Timer</h3>
                <span class="category">WOD timer · Fitness · Wear OS</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="problem">
              <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
              <p>
                The timer apps I tried had confusing screens, took too long to set up and were never as flexible as my
                workouts. Their digits were too small to read from across the room, and they would not work in the
                background when I switched to another app.
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="description">
              For Time, AMRAP, EMOM, Tabata and your own custom sequences, with huge high-contrast digits on phone, tablet
              and watch.
            </p>
            <ul class="chips">
              <li>5 timer modes</li>
              <li>Custom workouts</li>
              <li>Wear OS companion</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="actions">
              <a href={apps.crossfitTimer.href} class="btn btn-primary">See CrossFit Timer</a>
              <a href={apps.crossfitTimer.play} class="btn btn-outline">Get it on Google Play</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="card card-hr">
          <div class="card-text">
            <div class="app-title">
              <Image src={hrIcon} alt="" width={64} height={64} densities={[1, 2]} />
              <div>
                <h3>Heart Rate Monitor</h3>
                <span class="category">Live HR zones · Bluetooth sensors</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="zones" aria-hidden="true">
              <span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="problem">
              <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
              <p>
                My chest strap's own app was really bad. I wanted a richer, more beautiful one that also worked with my
                other sensors, and with my watch from another brand.
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="description">
              Connect any standard Bluetooth chest strap, armband or watch and see your zone second by second, then look
              back at every workout.
            </p>
            <ul class="chips">
              <li>Polar, Garmin, Wahoo, COROS</li>
              <li>Zones 1 to 5, live</li>
              <li>No account</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="actions">
              <a href={apps.heartrateMonitor.href} class="btn btn-primary">See Heart Rate Monitor</a>
              <a href={apps.heartrateMonitor.play} class="btn btn-outline">Get it on Google Play</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card-phones">
            <Phone src={hrLive} alt="Live heart rate at 157 bpm in zone 4" statusBar />
            <Phone src={hrSummary} alt="Workout summary with time in zones" statusBar class="offset" />
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="about" class="container about">
      <div class="about-title">
        <span class="eyebrow">Behind the studio</span>
        <h2>One developer, all the love.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-text">
        <p>
          Studio Bridoux AB is just me, Nicolas, a French Android engineer living in Stockholm. Every app is designed,
          built and looked after by one person.
        </p>
        <p>
          I love building on a platform that billions of people, me included, use every day, and I try to pay attention
          to the details: polished screens, smooth animations, and apps that go easy on your battery. Outside of work I
          travel and train a lot, which is exactly where these apps come from.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="btn btn-primary">Email me</a>
          <a href={githubUrl} class="btn btn-outline">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: #1d4ed8;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: #0b2a66;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #1d4ed8;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .btn-outline {
    border-color: #b8c6e0;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #0b2a66;
  }

  .btn-outline:hover {
    border-color: #0b2a66;
    color: #0b2a66;
  }

  .hero {
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-text {
    flex: 1 1 480px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .hero-text .eyebrow {
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .hero .btn {
    padding: 14px 24px;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .hero-phones {
    flex: 1 1 420px;
    min-width: 0;
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 6 / 5;
    --phone-border: #0b1220;
  }

  .hero-phones :global(.phone) {
    position: absolute;
    width: 36%;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 48px rgba(11, 42, 102, 0.18);
  }

  .hero-phones :global(.hero-left) {
    left: 2%;
    top: 14%;
    transform: rotate(-7deg);
  }

  .hero-phones :global(.hero-right) {
    right: 2%;
    top: 14%;
    transform: rotate(7deg);
  }

  .hero-phones :global(.hero-center) {
    left: 31%;
    top: 0;
    width: 38%;
    --phone-radius: 24px;
    box-shadow: 0 32px 64px rgba(11, 42, 102, 0.25);
  }

  .apps {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .apps-inner {
    padding-top: 96px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  .section-intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .section-intro p {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .card {
    border-radius: 28px;
    padding: 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .card-text {
    flex: 1 1 420px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .app-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .app-title :global(img) {
    width: 64px;
    height: 64px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    flex: none;
  }

  .app-title div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 28px;
  }

  .category {
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .problem {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .problem p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .description {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .card-phones {
    flex: 1 1 360px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .card-phones :global(.phone) {
    width: 44%;
    max-width: 220px;
  }

  .card-phones :global(.offset) {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .card-fp {
    background: #eaf1fd;
  }

  .card-fp .category,
  .card-fp .description {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .card-fp .chips li {
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .card-fp .btn-outline {
    border-color: #9db2d8;
  }

  .card-cf,
  .card-hr {
    color: #f2f4f8;
  }

  .card-cf h3,
  .card-hr h3,
  .card-cf .problem p,
  .card-hr .problem p {
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .card-cf {
    background: #111318;
    flex-wrap: wrap-reverse;
    --phone-border: #2a2f3a;
  }

  .card-cf .category {
    color: #b4bccb;
  }

  .card-cf .eyebrow {
    color: #9db8f5;
  }

  .card-cf .description {
    color: #c9d0dc;
  }

  .card-cf .chips li {
    background: #232836;
  }

  .card-cf .btn-primary {
    background: #9db8f5;
    color: #0b1220;
  }

  .card-cf .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #c7d6fa;
  }

  .card-cf .btn-outline {
    background: transparent;
    border-color: #3a4152;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .card-cf .btn-outline:hover {
    border-color: #9db8f5;
  }

  .card-hr {
    background: #0f1a17;
    --phone-border: #26332f;
  }

  .card-hr .category {
    color: #b4c4be;
  }

  .card-hr .eyebrow {
    color: #7fd3a0;
  }

  .card-hr .description {
    color: #c9d6d1;
  }

  .card-hr .chips li {
    background: #1c2b27;
  }

  .card-hr .btn-primary {
    background: #7fd3a0;
    color: #0b1a14;
  }

  .card-hr .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #b5e8c8;
  }

  .card-hr .btn-outline {
    background: transparent;
    border-color: #34483f;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .card-hr .btn-outline:hover {
    border-color: #7fd3a0;
  }

  .zones {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .zones span {
    height: 6px;
    flex: 1;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .zones span:nth-child(1) {
    background: #8e9ba8;
  }

  .zones span:nth-child(2) {
    background: #3b82c8;
  }

  .zones span:nth-child(3) {
    background: #2ea35a;
  }

  .zones span:nth-child(4) {
    background: #e08a1e;
  }

  .zones span:nth-child(5) {
    background: #d9403a;
  }

  .about {
    padding-top: 96px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 32px 72px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .about-title {
    flex: 1 1 380px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .about-title .eyebrow {
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .about-text {
    flex: 1 1 520px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .about-text p {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero {
      padding-top: 32px;
      padding-bottom: 64px;
    }

    .apps-inner,
    .about {
      padding-top: 64px;
      padding-bottom: 64px;
    }

    .card {
      padding: 24px;
      border-radius: 24px;
      gap: 32px;
    }

    .card-phones {
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .card-phones :global(.offset) {
      margin-top: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
